{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":311770,"duration_api_ms":364487,"num_turns":59,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"904e4d93-adde-4d38-9ea9-b424df2e62bc","total_cost_usd":2.2807599499999993,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67901,"cache_read_input_tokens":2465646,"output_tokens":9357,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67901,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":44,"outputTokens":9357,"cacheReadInputTokens":2465646,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67901,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.89134925,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3874,"outputTokens":11143,"cacheReadInputTokens":1940617,"cacheCreationInputTokens":108608,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3894107000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"The change to non-zero DIC rate defaults (respiration_dic_rate: 0.0→0.01875, photosynthesis_dic_rate: 0.0→0.075) breaks 7 existing closed-system carbon conservation tests across two test files:\n\n**budget_tracking.rs** (5 failures):\n- test_closed_system_c_conservation\n- test_closed_system_shrimp_mortality_conserves_n_and_c\n- test_trim_plants_and_leave_cuttings_preserves_n_and_c\n- test_trim_plants_and_remove_exports_n_and_c\n- test_clean_filter_routes_removed_microbes_to_dissolved_organics\n\n**budget_helpers.rs** (2 failures):\n- closed_system_n_and_c_conserved_via_helpers\n- trim_plants_and_leave_cuttings_is_closed_system_via_helpers\n\nRoot cause: The shared helper `close_budget_gas_exchange()` in budget_tracking.rs (line 21-30) zeroes reaeration/aeration but does NOT zero the DIC shortcut rates. Before this change, those rates defaulted to 0.0 so it was harmless. Now they default to non-zero values, injecting carbon into closed-system tests.\n\nFix: Add `state.process_params.respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.0;` and `state.process_params.photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.0;` to `close_budget_gas_exchange()`. The same fix is needed for the budget_helpers.rs test fixtures. The conservation_regression.rs tests already have `disable_dic_shortcuts()` and pass correctly — the pattern just wasn't propagated to all test files.","rationale":"This is a real regression: `cargo test` currently fails with 7 test failures. The DIC rate defaults were changed in both process.rs and default.toml but the closed-system test fixtures were only partially updated (only test_high_mortality was patched at line 1377-1384). The acceptance criteria require all conservation tests to pass."},{"body":"The water change test fixtures in both conservation_regression.rs (line 882-886) and e2e_conservation.rs (line 680-684) calculate `expected_n_export` using only dissolved N species (ammonia, nitrite, nitrate, DON), while the production budget code in water_change.rs:112-117 also includes `algae_nitrogen_mg(state.algae.suspended_biomass_g)`. Similarly, `expected_c_export` omits suspended algae carbon while water_change.rs:118-121 includes it.\n\nThis is currently safe because both fixtures zero `suspended_biomass_g`. However, it creates a maintenance trap: if any future change adds non-zero suspended algae to the water change fixture, the test's expected values will silently diverge from the actual budget calculation, and conservation assertions will fail for the wrong reason.\n\nFix: Either add a comment documenting the dependency (e.g., `// NOTE: expected_n_export omits suspended algae N — safe only because fixture sets suspended_biomass_g = 0.0`) or include the algae terms with the zero value to make the formula match the production code exactly.","rationale":"Test-production formula mismatch is a common source of confusing false failures when fixtures evolve. Documenting the implicit assumption or making formulas match prevents wasted debugging time."}],"summary":"Reviewed the DIC rate default changes (process.rs, default.toml), conservation regression tests, e2e conservation tests, budget tracking tests, and budget helpers tests. The stoichiometric values (C:O2 = 12:32 = 0.375) are correct, and the conservation_regression.rs and e2e tests all pass. However, the DIC rate change from 0.0 to non-zero defaults introduced a real regression: 7 tests across budget_tracking.rs and budget_helpers.rs now fail because their shared `close_budget_gas_exchange()` helper was not updated to zero the DIC shortcut rates. The fix applied to test_high_mortality (line 1377-1384) was not propagated to the shared helper used by other closed-system tests. Additionally, there is a minor maintenance risk where water change test expected-value formulas omit suspended algae terms that the production code includes (safe only because fixtures zero suspended algae). The intentional exclusion of `dissolved_feed_residue_g_total` from budget components is correct — it's a shadow counter that mirrors DOC/DON and is explicitly tested as excluded."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"82b7f5a7-9423-4612-a7b4-405730e11687"}
